<html>
<title>How do I play the Studio II homebrew games?</title> 
<body>

<h1>How do I play the Studio II homebrew games?</h1>

<p>
This section includes short instructions for most included <strong>homebrew</strong> ST2 files. In some cases more complete instructions can be found in the game directory. 
</p>

<p>
The descriptions below assume you are using a numeric keypad and have selected menu item <strong>Settings/Use Numeric Keypad</strong>. If this option is not selected, the alternative key is indicated in parentheses.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> For Player B, keys <tt>W</tt>, <tt>A</tt>, <tt>S</tt>, <tt>Z</tt> control direction and <tt>TAB</tt> is used to fire. These keys work both with and without the <strong>Use Numeric Keypad</strong> setting enabled.
</p>


<h2>Asteroids</h2>

<p>
Freeware game developed by Paul Robson.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
5             start
Up Arrow      move
Left Arrow    left
Right Arrow   right
SPACE         fire
</pre>


<h2>Berzerk</h2>

<p>
Freeware game developed by Paul Robson.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
5             start
Arrow Keys    move in 8 directions
              (pressing two move keys simultaneously moves diagonally)
SPACE + move  fire in walking direction
</pre>


<h2>Climber</h2>

<p>
Developed by Lee Romanow.
</p>

<p>
Press one of the following keys:
</p>

<pre>
3     Novice
4     Standard
5     Advanced
6     Expert
</pre>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Up Arrow      move up
Left Arrow    move left
Right Arrow   move right
Down Arrow    move down
</pre>


<h2>Combat</h2>

<p>
This is a version of the Atari 2600 game <strong>Combat</strong> for 2 players designed by Paul Robson. This game has 256 different game types (approximately 80 of which are unique, as some are duplicates).
</p>

<p>
Options include a tank or plane game, slow or fast missiles, short and long range missiles, and various playing areas. Various combinations are available.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
Left Arrow     left
Right Arrow    right
Up Arrow       forward / speed up (plane)
Down Arrow     backward / slow down (plane)
SPACE          fire

Player B
--------
Numpad 4 (A)   left
Numpad 6 (S)   right
Numpad 8 (W)   forward / speed up (plane)
Numpad 2 (Z)   backward / slow down (plane)
Numpad 0 (TAB) fire
</pre>

<p><strong>Start</strong></p>

<p>
The game will display G? in the middle of the screen. Enter the code of the game you want to play using keys <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt>. After entering the game code, press Numpad <tt>0</tt> (<tt>TAB</tt>) to start the game.
</p>

<p>
The winner is the first person to score 9 hits. Collision with everything is fatal.
</p>

<p><strong>Level Calculation</strong></p>

<p>
A complete list of levels is shown below. Here is how to work out your level. Start with zero. Then:
</p>

<pre>
+128  plane game (otherwise tank)
+64   long range missiles (otherwise short range)
+32   slow missiles (otherwise fast missiles)
+16   border around the screen
+8    tank defences
+4    defences + barriers
+2    balloons
+1    mines
</pre>

<p><strong>Note:</strong> For the last four options, only the first named option will work; you cannot have balloons *and* mines.</p>

<p><strong>Game Types</strong></p>

<p>
Here are the levels the game supports:
</p>

<pre>
Game   0 : Tank   :Short range Fast missiles.
Game   1 : Tank   :Short range Fast missiles. Minefield.
Game   2 : Tank   :Short range Fast missiles. Balloons.
Game   4 : Tank   :Short range Fast missiles. Full Terrain.
